  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would be located in a primarily residential area, and would not be located in a designated industrial zone. This would present significant conflict with the development plan, and fails to provide suitable justification for the need of this development in this area. Officers do not consider this appropriate for this setting. The proposal would not be located in a suitable location and would would conflict with the character of the area.&nbsp; The principle of development is therefore not supported, and is in conflict with:The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D1, D4, E4 and E7 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies SP2, SP5 and DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development would represent an inappropriate and incompatible use within a residential area, failing to preserve the character of the locality and resulting in harm to the character of the area, as well as moderate harm to the Becontree Estate as an NDHA. The proposal would therefore be contrary to:The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D1, D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies SPP6, SP2 and DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "In the absence of further information with regard to noise attenuation measures and mitigation, and given that the proposal would be located in a residential area, officers consider the proposed use to be inappropriate and result in harm to the amenity of neighbouring amenity and would therefore be contrary to:The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D6 and D14 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies DMD1, DMSI 13 and DME 1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "In the absence of further information with regard to vehicle movements, including larger vans and servicing vehicles, the proposal raises concerns regarding traffic generation, vehicle manoeuvring and noise and disturbances. The proposal has failed to acknowledge transport impacts, and it is likely the proposal would result in harm to highway safety. The proposal is therefore contrary to:The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies T1, T2 and T4 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies DMT1 and SP8 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "Given the absence of a detailed site plan, it is not possible to assess and determine the amount of habitat that would be lost. Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the proposed development would not result in harm to biodiversity in this instance. The proposal is therefore contrary to:Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (As amended)Policy DMNE 3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
